 sharing, committing, or pushing any `.md`, `.tex`, or `.pdf` artifact,\\nidentify the affected files and run the gate. Fix failures before delivery. If a failure is\\nintentionally left unresolved, say exactly which gate failed and why.\\n\\n## Quick Start\\n\\nFrom the repository root, run:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 path/to/style-gates/scripts/style_gate.py --changed\\n```\\n\\nBefore commit or push, prefer:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 path/to/style-gates/scripts/style_gate.py --staged\\npython3 path/to/style-gates/scripts/style_gate.py --changed --base origin/main\\n```\\n\\nFor a specific artifact:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 path/to/style-gates/scripts/style_gate.py report.md paper.tex slides.pdf\\n```\\n\\nUse `--strict-warnings` when the recipient wants warnings to block delivery.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. Determine scope:\\n   - For generated files, pass the exact output paths.\\n   - For a commit, use `--staged`.\\n   - For a branch or push, use `--changed --base origin/main` or the relevant upstream base.\\n   - For an initial audit, use `--all`.\\n2. Run the gate script.\\n3. Fix all errors. Treat warnings as review prompts unless `--strict-warnings` is required.\\n4. For LaTeX and PDFs, also use project-native validation when available:\\n   - Compile `.tex` with the repo\'s existing command or `latexmk`/`pdflatex`.\\n   - Open or inspect generated PDFs enough to confirm they are not blank, corrupt, or stale.\\n5. Re-run the gate after edits.\\n\\n## Human Review Gates\\n\\nThe script catches mechanical issues; still review these before sharing.\\n\\nMarkdown:\\n- Clear title and section hierarchy.\\n- No unresolved placeholders, merge markers, stale TODOs, or fake links.\\n- Tables, lists, math, and fenced code render plausibly.\\n- Claims with external facts have sources or are clearly marked as assumptions.\\n\\nLaTeX:\\n- The file compiles, or the reason it was not compiled is reported.\\n- No unresolved citations/references in the build log when a PDF is produced